        "client_msg_id": "fb9a57e1-2d08-408b-9072-aee29398447b",
        "text": "I think \"fork\" could be replaced better with \"evolve in a breaking way\", thus distinguishing splitting evolution from breaking evolution and then breaking ecosystems. I mean, a fork shouldn't actually break anything if you're on the fork, it should be backwards compatible down the tree.",
